{"content":[{"c":["PAROUSIA*"],"t":"p"},{"c":["Transliteration of a Greek word meaning “presence,” “arrival,” “appearance,” or “coming.” While it is used often with reference to people (",{"r":"1Cor.16.17","t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 16:17"},"; ",{"r":"2Cor.7.6","t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 7:6"},"; ",{"r":"2Cor.10.10","t":"ref","v":"10:10"},"; ",{"r":"Phil.1.26","t":"ref","v":"Phil 1:26"},"; ",{"r":"Phil.2.12","t":"ref","v":"2:12"},") and once with reference to the Antichrist (",{"r":"2Thes.2.9","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:9"},"), the word is employed most frequently with reference to Christ (",{"r":"Matt.24.3,27,37-39","t":"ref","v":"Mt 24:3, 27, 37-39"},"; ",{"r":"1Cor.15.23","t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:23"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.2.19","t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 2:19"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.3.13","t":"ref","v":"3:13"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.4.15","t":"ref","v":"4:15"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.5.23","t":"ref","v":"5:23"},"; ",{"r":"2Thes.2.1,8","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:1, 8"},"). Consequently, the Parousia has come to denote the second coming of Christ at the end of the ages."],"t":"p"},{"c":["Paul was probably responsible for the technical emphasis on Christ’s return. While rejecting all attempts to calculate the time (",{"r":"1Thes.5.1-2","t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 5:1-2"},"; ",{"r":"2Thes.2.2-3","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 2:2-3"},"; cf. ",{"r":"Matt.24.4-36","t":"ref","v":"Mt 24:4-36"},"), he nonetheless paints a vivid picture of the Parousia (",{"r":"1Thes.4.13-18","t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 4:13-18"},"; ",{"r":"2Thes.1.7-2.8","t":"ref","v":"2 Thes 1:7–2:8"},"; see also ",{"r":"1Cor.15.20-28,50-55","t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:20-28, 50-55"},"). According to his teaching, it will be a personal, visible, sudden, and glorious coming (",{"r":"1Cor.15.23","t":"ref","v":"1 Cor 15:23"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.2.19","t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 2:19"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.3.13","t":"ref","v":"3:13"},"; ",{"r":"1Thes.4.15-17","t":"ref","v":"4:15-17"},"). Though apparently he felt he and his readers would experience Christ’s return (",{"r":"1Thes.4.15","t":"ref","v":"1 Thes 4:15"},"; cf. ",{"r":"Rom.8.23","t":"ref","v":"Rom 8:23"},"; ",{"r":"Rom.13.11","t":"ref","v":"13:11"},"), his approaching martyrdom caused him to moderate his thinking (",{"r":"Phil.1.23","t":"ref","v":"Phil 1:23"},"). James, also sensing the delay in Christ’s return, called for patience (",{"r":"Jas.5.7-8","t":"ref","v":"Jas 5:7-8"},"). Peter, too, cautioned against allowing the delay to create doubt (",{"r":"2Pet.3.8-10","t":"ref","v":"2 Pt 3:8-10"},"). The message is not myth (",{"r":"2Pet.1.16","t":"ref","v":"2 Pt 1:16"},"), and scoffers will be silenced (",{"r":"2Pet.3.3-4","t":"ref","v":"3:3-4"},"). John encouraged consistent faith lest the believer be put to shame at his coming (",{"r":"1Jn.2.28","t":"ref","v":"1 Jn 2:28"},")."],"t":"p"},{"c":[{"t":"em","v":"See also"}," ",{"id":"Eschatology_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Eschatology"},"; ",{"id":"SecondComingofChrist_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Second Coming of Christ"},"."],"t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Parousia","provenance":{"philippiansReferences":["Phil.1.23","Phil.1.26","Phil.2.12"],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"b6d6f5a55d66fb7b73093d02d8486f8aa7f20e44b5349324cdfaeca991ddbffc","sourceItemName":"Parousia","sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"title":"Parousia*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}